   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT granting retroactive tier IV status in the New York state and local\nemployees' retirement system to Kimberly Kinblom",
    "basePrintNo": "S9026",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9026-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9026\n\nSPONSOR: STEC\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act granting retroactive tier IV status in the New York state and\nlocal employees' retirement system to Kimberly Kinblom\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAn act granting retroactive tier IV status in the New York state and\nlocal employees' retirement system to Kimberly Kinblom\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Permits Kimberly Kinblom to participate in Tier IV of the\nNew York State and Local Employee's retirement system and backdates her\nretirement membership to when she was first employed by the City of\nPlattsburgh on June 28, 2004. This section gives Ms. Kimberly Kinblom a\nyear from the effective date to apply for these changes.\n\nSection 2 - Places all costs associated with implementation on the State\nof New York.\n\nSection 3- Provides effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nKimberly Kinblom was first employed by the City of Plattsburgh on June\n28, 2004 and is now employed by Clinton County. When she filled out her\nretirement paperwork when she started her job with the county, she was\ninformed that her retirement paperwork from her previous job had not\nbeen filed due to no fault of her own. This bill would correct this\nmistake and give Ms. Kinblom for the years she has already worked as a\nlocal employee.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nAll costs will be borne by Clinton County. See fiscal note\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nEffective immediately\n",
